# macOS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.textClipping

# Third-party course materials. The textbook chapter is a copyrighted work
# published by its publisher, not ours to redistribute — keep it locally, out
# of version control, even in a private repository.
Ch 1..pdf
Ch. 2.docx
Ch*.pdf
Ch*.docx
*.epub

# Institutional and assessment documents. These carry the school name, the
# course code, and the wording of a graded case. The module itself is written
# to contain none of that, and committing the source documents would put it
# all back. Keep them beside the repo, not inside it.
*Signature Assignment*.docx
Course Objectives*.docx
*Management-Information-Systems.pdf
Syllabus*.pdf

# The supplied course materials, kept beside the working copy rather than in it. Everything in here is either
# the publisher's chapter text or institutional paperwork: the textbook chapters, the eleven course objectives,
# and the signature assignment whose case name is the reserved term src/check.mjs --release refuses to ship.
# Ignoring the directory rather than each file means a new document dropped in here cannot be swept in by a
# `git add -A` before anyone notices it.
book/

# Terms reserved to a live assessment, checked by src/check.mjs but never
# committed — naming them here would be the same leak by another route.
src/forbidden.local.txt

# Instructor-only grading guidance for the practice case study. The student-facing page sits right
# beside this file, so keep the model-answer notes out of git rather than trust a manual review of
# every future `git add` to catch it. Commit only when explicitly released.
practice-case-study/instructor-notes*.md

# The midterm's answer key, for exactly the same reason and with less room for error: the exam page
# is committed and the key sits beside it. The page itself carries no answers, only a weights
# comment, because a student can read its source.
midterm-instructor-key*.md
midterm-answer-key*.md
practice-final-instructor-key*.md
practice-final-answer-key*.md

# Build scratch
/tmp/
*.tmp.html
